You and the Architect are flung back into the office after realizing the game was impossible to beat...
join "The Architect" center [animation="Slide In Down" length="1.3"]
"The Architect": "Okay. So clearly that game is going to take a minute to sort itself out, I'll have someone go and fix the AI, oh wait I'm the AI haha."
"The Architect": "In the mean time why don't we try out another game, maybe something a bit more involved?"
"The Architect": "Tell me, what season do you like the most?"
- Summer! | [="@"]
- Winter! | [="@"]
- Spring! | [="@"]
"The Architect": "ooooh very good, I really like none of them myself, since I don't go outside much anymore..."
"The Architect": "A few years ago there was this one platforming game I used to play before becoming an architect that I spent so much time playing. Of course now, I don't have much time for that, while making a game for new players..."
"The Architect": "I HAVE AN IDEA! What if I made that game here for you to play? That would be a good start, they say to 'practice what you play' and what would be a better way to practice than to play that game!"
Without a chance to say anything else the architect snaps their fingers and the screen rotates upwards toward the office ceiling where a large flat screen is mounted precariously.
[background arg="res://Assets/my assets/environment/industrial-bg.png" fade="0.0"]
"The Architect": "This is the best screen to play this game on just you wait!"
The screen turns on with out a sound, the LED's come to life with a 90's style platformer featuring a middle aged man in some sort of jumpsuit. The opening screen has the word "Start" flashing in large red letters.
"The Architect": "Why don't you grab this controller and get to playing you'll have to let me know what you think of it as you play!"
The architect is shaking with excitment.
